ready: 1
kind: module
id: consolidation
name: Consolidation
summary: >-
  Turns experience into higher layers of memory through sleep runs, processing, and the suggestion
  queue, within a daily model budget.
notes: >-
  Sleep runs appraise, replay, and extract; processing transitions carry raw captures up to
  values; held changes wait in the suggestion queue for review; and the agent can ask for a
  reflection scaffold.
runs_in:
  - sys.daemon
  - sys.cli
  - sys.python
owns:
  - Suggestions and their review (DATA-SUGGESTION)
  - Per-transition processing marks (DATA-TRANSITION-MARK)
  - Maintenance runs and the daily model budget (DATA-RUN)
  - Filing, replay, and promotion rules
invariants:
  - At most one maintenance run per stack at a time.
  - Every processing transition sees every eligible source exactly once.
  - Identity layers from processing or sleep always wait for review.
  - Daily model spend never exceeds the budget by more than one request.
rationale: >-
  The working agent should spend no effort on memory upkeep, so consolidation runs on its own
  schedule while the agent is idle. Explicit processing calls stay for agents and owners who
  want to drive it, and both paths share one set of transitions, rules, and marks so they never
  disagree about what has been processed.


  Emotion files memory here: the appraisal label of each replayed episode decides which kind
  of memory it may become, so a near-disaster becomes a guardrail and a correction becomes a
  preference rather than a generic note.
